:name: nRF52840 DK
:description: Runs a Zephyr ELF on Renode's nRF52840 model, with the DK's sw0 and led0.
:
: Set $elf to an absolute path before including this script. There is no `start`, so
: button_led.robot can attach its testers first. By hand, from apps/renode-test:
:
:   renode --console --disable-xwt -e "\$elf=@$PWD/build/zephyr/zephyr.elf; include @run_nrf52.resc; start"
:
: Renode's own nrf52840dk_nrf52840.repl is not used: its buttons lack `invert: true`, so
: the active-low sw0 reads as held from boot. The button and LED below match the DK.

set platform
"""
using "platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl"

gpio0:
    13 -> led0@0

led0: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpio0 13
    invert: true

sw0: Miscellaneous.Button @ gpio0 11
    invert: true
    -> gpio0@11
"""

mach create "nrf52840"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString $platform

showAnalyzer sysbus.uart0

sysbus LoadELF $elf
